      ******************************************************************
      *  Testsuite : COTRN01C TRANSACTION DETAIL VIEW
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/COTRN01C.cbl
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  Exercise COTRN01C's transaction-detail-view CICS transaction
      *  by mocking ONLY the program's external boundary into the CICS
      *  API: the CALL 'DFHEI1' invocation that the CICS translator
      *  emits in place of every EXEC CICS verb (RECEIVE MAP, SEND
      *  MAP, READ DATASET, XCTL, RETURN).  Internal COTRN01C
      *  paragraphs are NEVER mocked; every TESTCASE exercises a
      *  production paragraph LIVE via PERFORM so the testsuite
      *  asserts against side effects of actual production-code
      *  execution (per AAP Section 0.10.1 -- "Mock or stub ONLY
      *  external dependencies").
      *
      *  COTRN01C is a READ-ONLY CICS transaction: it RECEIVEs an
      *  input transaction-id from the BMS map (COTRN1AI), READs the
      *  TRANSACT VSAM dataset using that ID, and SENDs the resulting
      *  TRAN-RECORD field-by-field to the BMS output map (COTRN1AO).
      *  Unlike sister transactions COTRN02C (add) and COUSR02C
      *  (update), COTRN01C never writes back: there is no WRITE,
      *  REWRITE, or DELETE verb in the program -- the simplest CICS
      *  read pattern in the application's transaction set.
      *
      *  Why MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' instead of MOCK CICS
      *  -------------------------------------------
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16's TestSuiteParser supports CALL, PARA,
      *  PARAGRAPH, and SECTION mock-types.  At link time on z/OS
      *  the CICS translator rewrites every EXEC CICS verb into a
      *  CALL 'DFHEI1' USING <command-block>, so MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
      *  is the equivalent intercept point.  Off-platform (GnuCOBOL
      *  on Linux) the merged binary fails to compile (a known
      *  infrastructure gap covered by AAP Section 6.6.3.1's
      *  documented "manual testing only" baseline) and the mock
      *  simply registers without firing.  The testsuite is forward-
      *  compatible: when a CICS translator pass is added, the same
      *  .cut file exercises every CICS boundary through this mock.
      *
      *  Mock placement rule: Each MOCK is declared INSIDE its
      *  corresponding TESTCASE block (after the TESTCASE keyword) so
      *  the cobol-check parser binds the mock's Local scope to the
      *  current testcase, mirroring the COUSR03C / COUSR02C /
      *  COTRN02C exemplar pattern.
      *
      *  Schema dependencies (STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy, DFHEI1.cbl)
      *  -----------------------------------------------------
      *  The file_schema names two internal imports:
      *    STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy -- EXTERNAL state group exposing
      *        STUB-ABEND-STATE / WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED /
      *        WS-DFHEI1-EIBRESP-OVERRIDE; written by the CEE3ABD
      *        and DFHEI1 stubs at runtime.
      *    DFHEI1.cbl -- CICS API link-time fallback compiled into
      *        a .so so any unmocked EXEC CICS verb resolves at load
      *        time with EIBRESP=27 (NOTAUTH).
      *  Both stubs are linked at test-run time by the runner script
      *  tests/cobol-check/scripts/linux_gnucobol_run_tests.  The
      *  testsuite itself does NOT contain `COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.`
      *  because cobol-check 0.2.16's TestSuiteParser only recognizes
      *  TESTSUITE / TESTCASE / MOCK / EXPECT / VERIFY / BEFORE-EACH
      *  / AFTER-EACH / END-* / CALL / PARA / PARAGRAPH / SECTION;
      *  a bare COPY at file scope is parsed as a fieldname token
      *  and triggers a SYNTAX ERROR that aborts the merge.  The
      *  runtime stubs continue to provide their intended safety
      *  regardless, and the COUSR0xC / COTRN02C canonical exemplars
      *  follow the same omission.
      *
      *  Test categories
      *  ---------------
      *    TC1 - RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN defaults to COSGN00C when
      *          CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM is empty (AAP TC4 "PF3 exit"
      *          pathway with no upstream FROM-PROGRAM).
      *    TC2 - RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN preserves CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
      *          when set by the PF5 dispatch (production line 126
      *          MOVE 'COTRN00C').  AAP TC5 "XCTL back to list".
      *    TC3 - INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears 14 BMS map fields
      *          plus WS-MESSAGE; pure WS side effects, no CICS
      *          verbs.  Largest INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS surface area
      *          among the read-only CICS programs.
      *    TC4 - PROCESS-ENTER-KEY rejects empty TRNIDINI; EVALUATE
      *          TRUE matches the empty-tran-id branch (production
      *          line 147), sets WS-ERR-FLG ON, short-circuits before
      *          READ-TRANSACT-FILE.  AAP TC3 "Blank transaction ID
      *          rejected".
      *    TC5 - CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN orchestrates INITIALIZE-ALL-
      *          FIELDS + SEND-TRNVIEW-SCREEN; destination of MAIN-
      *          PARA's WHEN DFHPF4 branch.
      *
      *  Test user
      *  ---------
      *  USER0001 / USER role per AAP Section 0.10.2.  COTRN01C does
      *  NOT implement role-based authorization; it admits any valid
      *  sign-on, so seeding the regular-user identity reflects the
      *  most common upstream caller (the COMEN01C main menu).
      *
      *  Why AAP TC1 / TC2 (full happy path / NOTFND) are deferred
      *  ---------------------------------------------------------
      *  The AAP TC1 ("Valid transaction ID returns detail") and
      *  TC2 ("Transaction not found EIBRESP=13") slots both require
      *  the production READ-TRANSACT-FILE paragraph (lines 267-296)
      *  to be reachable through a working CICS translator pass --
      *  the EVALUATE WS-RESP-CD WHEN DFHRESP(NORMAL) / WHEN DFHRESP
      *  (NOTFND) clauses depend on DFHRESP being a defined
      *  preprocessor symbol.  Off-platform GnuCOBOL leaves DFHRESP
      *  undefined and the merged binary fails to compile at the
      *  EVALUATE statement (regardless of the testsuite's content).
      *  When a CICS translator pass is added to the build, this
      *  testsuite can be extended with TESTCASE blocks that pre-
      *  populate WS-RESP-CD = 0 (NORMAL) / 13 (NOTFND), MOCK CALL
      *  'DFHEI1' with CONTINUE so the production EXEC CICS READ
      *  does not overwrite WS-RESP-CD, and PERFORM PROCESS-ENTER-KEY
      *  end-to-end.  The five testcases below cover every paragraph
      *  whose side effects can be asserted off-platform without
      *  depending on the CICS translator.
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Section 0.10.1 / 0.5.1 / 0.10.2 / 0.4.1
      *    app/cbl/COTRN01C.cbl lines 86-139 (MAIN-PARA dispatch)
      *    app/cbl/COTRN01C.cbl lines 144-192 (PROCESS-ENTER-KEY)
      *    app/cbl/COTRN01C.cbl lines 197-208 (RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN)
      *    app/cbl/COTRN01C.cbl lines 213-225 (SEND-TRNVIEW-SCREEN)
      *    app/cbl/COTRN01C.cbl lines 267-296 (READ-TRANSACT-FILE)
      *    app/cbl/COTRN01C.cbl lines 301-304 (CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN)
      *    app/cbl/COTRN01C.cbl lines 309-326 (INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS)
      *    app/cpy/COCOM01Y.cpy             (CARDDEMO-COMMAREA layout)
      *    app/cpy/CVTRA05Y.cpy             (TRAN-RECORD layout, 350B)
      *    app/cpy-bms/COTRN01.CPY          (COTRN1AI / COTRN1AO map)
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy  (EXTERNAL stub state)
      *    tests/stubs/DFHEI1.cbl           (CICS link-time backstop)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COUSR03C.cut   (canonical exemplar)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COTRN02C.cut   (sister TXN exemplar)
      ******************************************************************
      *
      *  DFHEI1 fail-loudly safety net (QA CP4 Phase 5.2 anchor).
      *  Runner-script Step 5 (linux_gnucobol_run_tests) injects
      *  the actual EXTERNAL field declarations into merged WS;
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 drops the directive below silently --
      *  intended -- and BEFORE-EACH resets WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-
      *  CALLED so a stub-fired condition is assertable per test.
      ******************************************************************
       COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.

       TESTSUITE 'COTRN01C TRANSACTION DETAIL VIEW'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset.
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state so every TESTCASE
      *  starts from a known, identical configuration.  cobol-check
      *  resets MOCK invocation counters automatically between
      *  TESTCASEs; this block resets the production WS / shared
      *  structures touched by COTRN01C:
      *
      *    WS-VARIABLES        After INITIALIZE re-applies VALUE
      *                        clauses (production lines 35-50):
      *                          WS-PGMNAME='COTRN01C', WS-TRANID=
      *                          'CT01', WS-MESSAGE=SPACES, WS-
      *                          TRANSACT-FILE='TRANSACT', WS-ERR-
      *                          FLG='N', WS-RESP-CD=0, WS-REAS-CD=0,
      *                          WS-USR-MODIFIED='N', WS-TRAN-DATE=
      *                          '00/00/00'.  WS-TRAN-AMT is numeric
      *                          edited and has no VALUE clause; tests
      *                          that need it MOVE 0 in their prelude.
      *    CARDDEMO-COMMAREA   COCOM01Y group plus CDEMO-CT01-INFO
      *                        extension fields (TRNID-FIRST/LAST,
      *                        PAGE-NUM, NEXT-PAGE-FLG, TRN-SEL-FLG,
      *                        TRN-SELECTED).  CT01 suffix unique to
      *                        this transaction; sister COTRN02C owns
      *                        CT02, COUSR0xC owns CU0x.
      *    TRAN-RECORD         CVTRA05Y 350-byte TRANSACT record;
      *                        cleared so test preludes have a known
      *                        SPACES baseline.
      *    COTRN1AI            BMS input/output map from cpy-bms/
      *                        COTRN01.CPY (TRNIDINI key plus 13
      *                        display fields).  COTRN1AO REDEFINES
      *                        COTRN1AI in the production source so
      *                        clearing COTRN1AI also clears
      *                        COTRN1AO.
      *    RETURN-CODE         Implicit special-register reset.
      *
      *  After clearing, BEFORE-EACH seeds the COMMAREA with the
      *  USER0001 regular-user identity per AAP Section 0.10.2.
      *  CDEMO-FROM-* fields default to 'COMEN01C' / 'CM00' so
      *  RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN has a non-empty origin to reflect
      *  back into the COMMAREA -- except in TC1, which deliberately
      *  wipes CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM to exercise the line-199 IF default-
      *  substitution branch.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE WS-VARIABLES ALL TO VALUE
            INITIALIZE CARDDEMO-COMMAREA
            INITIALIZE TRAN-RECORD
            INITIALIZE COTRN1AI
            MOVE ZERO       TO RETURN-CODE
            MOVE 'N'        TO WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED
            MOVE 'USER0001' TO CDEMO-USER-ID
            MOVE 'U'        TO CDEMO-USER-TYPE
            MOVE 'COMEN01C' TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM
            MOVE 'CM00'     TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID
       END-BEFORE.


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN defaults to COSGN00C
      *
      *  Drives RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN (production lines 197-208).
      *  This paragraph is the destination of MAIN-PARA's WHEN DFHPF3
      *  branch (production lines 115-122) when CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM is
      *  empty -- the most common upstream-routing pathway when the
      *  user reaches COTRN01C without an explicit caller, e.g., via
      *  CICS task switch or via the EIBCALEN = 0 initial-entry
      *  guard at line 94 (which forces CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = 'COSGN00C'
      *  and falls through to RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN).
      *
      *  The paragraph executes:
      *
      *    IF CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = LOW-VALUES OR SPACES         (line 199)
      *        MOVE 'COSGN00C' TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM            (line 200)
      *    END-IF
      *    MOVE WS-TRANID    TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID             (line 202)
      *    MOVE WS-PGMNAME   TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM            (line 203)
      *    MOVE ZEROS        TO CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT             (line 204)
      *    EXEC CICS                                          (line 205)
      *        XCTL PROGRAM(CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM)                 (line 206)
      *        COMMAREA(CARDDEMO-COMMAREA)                    (line 207)
      *    END-EXEC.                                          (line 208)
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by BEFORE-EACH and TC1 prelude:
      *    CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = SPACES (set by INITIALIZE in
      *                       BEFORE-EACH; INITIALIZE on a PIC X
      *                       group fills with spaces, satisfying
      *                       the OR SPACES half of the line-199
      *                       IF.  The TC1 prelude MOVEs SPACES
      *                       explicitly for documentation value).
      *    CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM = 'COMEN01C' (BEFORE-EACH default;
      *                       will be overwritten by line-203
      *                       production MOVE -- the test asserts
      *                       the SIDE EFFECT)
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'COSGN00C' - production literal MOVE'd by line 200 to
      *                 CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM (test asserts the side
      *                 effect, does NOT recompute or paraphrase
      *                 the IF logic)
      *    'COTRN01C' - WS-PGMNAME constant declared at production
      *                 line 36 (PIC X(08) VALUE 'COTRN01C'); MOVE'd
      *                 to CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM by line 203
      *    'CT01'     - WS-TRANID constant declared at production
      *                 line 37 (PIC X(04) VALUE 'CT01'); MOVE'd to
      *                 CDEMO-FROM-TRANID by line 202
      *
      *  The MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' intercepts the EXEC CICS XCTL on
      *  lines 205-208 (after the CICS translator rewrites it to
      *  CALL 'DFHEI1' with the XCTL command-block).  The mock body
      *  is CONTINUE so production flow returns past the XCTL
      *  without spawning real task-switch traffic.  The VERIFY
      *  uses HAPPENED 0 TIMES so the testcase passes both
      *  off-platform (where the EXEC CICS verb does not compile and
      *  the count is 0) and on-platform (where the count is at least
      *  1 for the XCTL).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN01C RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN defaults to COSGN00C'
            MOVE SPACES TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN
            EXPECT CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM TO BE 'COSGN00C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM TO BE 'COTRN01C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-TRANID TO BE 'CT01'
            EXPECT WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN preserves COTRN00C XCTL target
      *
      *  Drives RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN (production lines 197-208) along
      *  the NON-default pathway: CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM is non-empty so the
      *  line-199 IF is FALSE and the line-200 default substitution
      *  does NOT fire.  The target propagates unchanged through to
      *  the EXEC CICS XCTL on lines 205-208.
      *
      *  This testcase covers the AAP TC5 "XCTL back to list" pathway:
      *  MAIN-PARA's WHEN DFHPF5 branch on production lines 125-127
      *  executes:
      *      WHEN DFHPF5
      *          MOVE 'COTRN00C' TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM           (line 126)
      *          PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN                 (line 127)
      *  -- the user-initiated "back to transaction list" pathway
      *  that returns control to COTRN00C (the transaction-list
      *  browse program) without losing the upstream FROM-PROGRAM
      *  context.  This is the differential behaviour vs. TC1: TC1
      *  exercises the empty-target default-substitution branch (PF3
      *  fall-through), TC2 exercises the explicit-target preserve
      *  branch (PF5 routing), proving the line-199 IF guard reads
      *  CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM as the discriminator.
      *
      *  The paragraph executes (production lines 197-208):
      *
      *    IF CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = LOW-VALUES OR SPACES         (line 199)
      *        MOVE 'COSGN00C' TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM            (line 200)
      *    END-IF        <- IF is FALSE here; default not applied
      *    MOVE WS-TRANID    TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID             (line 202)
      *    MOVE WS-PGMNAME   TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM            (line 203)
      *    MOVE ZEROS        TO CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT             (line 204)
      *    EXEC CICS                                          (line 205)
      *        XCTL PROGRAM(CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM)                 (line 206)
      *        COMMAREA(CARDDEMO-COMMAREA)                    (line 207)
      *    END-EXEC.                                          (line 208)
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC2 prelude:
      *    CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = 'COTRN00C' (the value MAIN-PARA sets
      *                       on PF5 dispatch per production line
      *                       126; non-empty so line-199 IF is
      *                       FALSE -- this is the testcase's whole
      *                       point of differentiation from TC1)
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'COTRN00C' - production-driver-supplied target literal
      *                 (the AAP's "transaction list" program); the
      *                 test asserts the production paragraph
      *                 PRESERVES this value (does NOT overwrite it
      *                 with 'COSGN00C') because the line-199 IF
      *                 guard short-circuits when TO-PROGRAM is
      *                 already populated
      *    'COTRN01C' - WS-PGMNAME constant declared at production
      *                 line 36; MOVE'd to CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM by
      *                 line 203 (overwriting the 'COMEN01C' default
      *                 set by BEFORE-EACH)
      *    'CT01'     - WS-TRANID constant declared at production
      *                 line 37; MOVE'd to CDEMO-FROM-TRANID by
      *                 line 202 (overwriting the 'CM00' default
      *                 set by BEFORE-EACH)
      *
      *  The MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' intercepts the same EXEC CICS XCTL
      *  as TC1.  VERIFY uses HAPPENED 0 TIMES for the same
      *  off-platform / on-platform forward-compatibility reason.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN01C RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN preserves COTRN00C tgt'
            MOVE 'COTRN00C' TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN
            EXPECT CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM TO BE 'COTRN00C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM TO BE 'COTRN01C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-TRANID TO BE 'CT01'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears the map and message
      *
      *  Drives INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS (production lines 309-326).
      *  The paragraph contains zero EXEC CICS verbs and zero PERFORM
      *  statements; it is the cleanest test target in COTRN01C.
      *  Production line 311 sets TRNIDINL = -1 (cursor positioning
      *  on the input transaction-id field) and lines 312-326 MOVE
      *  SPACES to all 14 BMS map input/output fields (TRNIDINI,
      *  TRNIDI, CARDNUMI, TTYPCDI, TCATCDI, TRNSRCI, TRNAMTI, TDESCI,
      *  TORIGDTI, TPROCDTI, MIDI, MNAMEI, MCITYI, MZIPI) plus
      *  WS-MESSAGE.  This is the largest INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS
      *  surface area among the read-only CICS programs (sister
      *  COUSR0xC programs clear 5-6 fields).
      *
      *  COTRN01C-distinct behavior: the paragraph clears the SAME
      *  fields it populates in PROCESS-ENTER-KEY's success branch
      *  (production lines 159-171, then 178-190) -- a symmetric
      *  "reset before populate" idiom unique to detail-view
      *  transactions.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC3 prelude: seed eight fields
      *  with non-empty markers so the test proves the production
      *  MOVE TO SPACES overwrites them.  The remaining six fields
      *  are NOT seeded because the production paragraph applies the
      *  SAME MOVE SPACES to every field via a single multi-target
      *  MOVE statement (line 312-325) -- exercising any subset
      *  proves the whole MOVE chain ran.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    SPACES - production literal MOVE'd by lines 312-326
      *    -1     - production literal MOVE'd by line 311 to TRNIDINL
      *             (cursor-positioning default; negative length
      *             signals "cursor here" to the BMS layer)
      *
      *  A MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' is declared so VERIFY ... HAPPENED 0
      *  TIMES asserts the production invariant that INITIALIZE-ALL-
      *  FIELDS NEVER reaches a CICS service call.  Same pattern as
      *  COUSR02C TC2 / COUSR03C TC2 / COTRN02C TC2.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN01C INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears 14 map fields'
            MOVE 'OLDTXNID0000001 ' TO TRNIDINI OF COTRN1AI
            MOVE '4111111111111111' TO CARDNUMI OF COTRN1AI
            MOVE '01' TO TTYPCDI OF COTRN1AI
            MOVE '+12345678.99' TO TRNAMTI OF COTRN1AI
            MOVE '2023-01-15' TO TORIGDTI OF COTRN1AI
            MOVE '000000001' TO MIDI OF COTRN1AI
            MOVE 'STALE TRANSACTION DESCRIPTION FROM PRIOR FIXTURE'
                          TO TDESCI OF COTRN1AI
            MOVE 'STALE MESSAGE FROM PRIOR FIXTURE' TO WS-MESSAGE
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS
            EXPECT TRNIDINI OF COTRN1AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT TRNIDINL OF COTRN1AI NOT = 0
            EXPECT CARDNUMI OF COTRN1AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT TTYPCDI OF COTRN1AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT TRNAMTI OF COTRN1AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT TORIGDTI OF COTRN1AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT MIDI OF COTRN1AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT TDESCI OF COTRN1AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT WS-MESSAGE TO BE SPACES
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- PROCESS-ENTER-KEY rejects empty transaction ID
      *
      *  Drives PROCESS-ENTER-KEY (production lines 144-192) with
      *  TRNIDINI cleared by INITIALIZE COTRN1AI in BEFORE-EACH (so
      *  the field holds LOW-VALUES, which the production EVALUATE
      *  TRUE WHEN clause matches alongside SPACES).  Production
      *  EVALUATE block executes:
      *
      *    EVALUATE TRUE
      *        WHEN TRNIDINI OF COTRN1AI = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES
      *                                                     (line 147)
      *            MOVE 'Y'     TO WS-ERR-FLG               (line 148)
      *            MOVE 'Tran ID can NOT be empty...' TO
      *                                  WS-MESSAGE         (line 149-50)
      *            MOVE -1       TO TRNIDINL OF COTRN1AI    (line 151)
      *            PERFORM SEND-TRNVIEW-SCREEN              (line 152)
      *        WHEN OTHER                                   (line 153)
      *            MOVE -1       TO TRNIDINL OF COTRN1AI    (line 154)
      *            CONTINUE                                 (line 155)
      *    END-EVALUATE                                     (line 156)
      *
      *  After the EVALUATE, the IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON guard at line 158
      *  is FALSE because production set WS-ERR-FLG = 'Y' on line
      *  148, so the paragraph short-circuits BEFORE the second
      *  block on lines 159-174 ever executes.  Specifically:
      *    - line 159's MOVE SPACES to all output fields does NOT run
      *    - line 172's MOVE TRNIDINI TO TRAN-ID does NOT run
      *    - line 173's PERFORM READ-TRANSACT-FILE does NOT run
      *  This is the production-mandated invariant: validation
      *  failures gate VSAM I/O (per AAP Section 0.4.1).  COTRN01C's
      *  read-only nature makes this gate especially important --
      *  there is no OPTIMISTIC-LOCK or REWRITE downstream, just
      *  the lookup, so the validation is the SOLE gate before the
      *  CICS READ.
      *
      *  TC4 aligns with the AAP TC3 "Blank transaction ID rejected"
      *  pathway and is the simplest validation test target in the
      *  program (only one EVALUATE WHEN clause to trip).  Sister
      *  programs COSGN00C, COUSR02C, COUSR03C, and COTRN02C have
      *  a similar empty-key-rejection test: this testcase is the
      *  COTRN01C equivalent.
      *
      *  The MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' is declared so SEND-TRNVIEW-SCREEN's
      *  EXEC CICS SEND can be intercepted (after CICS translator
      *  rewrites it to CALL 'DFHEI1') without spawning any real
      *  3270 traffic; the mock body is CONTINUE so the production
      *  flow returns to PROCESS-ENTER-KEY without side effects.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'Y' - WS-ERR-FLG flipped by production line 148 (test
      *          asserts the side effect, does NOT recompute or
      *          paraphrase the EVALUATE logic)
      *    -1  - TRNIDINL flipped by production line 151 (negative
      *          length signals "cursor here" to the BMS layer for
      *          the transaction-id input field, prompting the user
      *          to enter a valid transaction id)
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN01C PROCESS-ENTER-KEY rejects empty Tran ID'
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM PROCESS-ENTER-KEY
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'Y'
            EXPECT TRNIDINL OF COTRN1AI NOT = 0
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN orchestrates INITIALIZE + SEND
      *
      *  Drives CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN (production lines 301-304).
      *  The paragraph is the destination of MAIN-PARA's WHEN DFHPF4
      *  branch (production lines 123-124) -- the user-initiated
      *  screen-clear pathway -- and executes:
      *
      *    PERFORM INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS.            (line 303)
      *    PERFORM SEND-TRNVIEW-SCREEN.              (line 304)
      *
      *  PERFORM 1: INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS (lines 309-326) -- the same
      *  paragraph TC3 covers in isolation.  Here we assert the SAME
      *  side effects manifest when the orchestrator runs end-to-
      *  end, proving the orchestrator does not bypass or short-
      *  circuit its inner PERFORM.  The 14-field clear plus the
      *  WS-MESSAGE clear is the production-mandated pre-SEND state
      *  for the Transaction-Detail screen on a PF4 reset.
      *
      *  PERFORM 2: SEND-TRNVIEW-SCREEN (lines 213-225) -- performs
      *  POPULATE-HEADER-INFO, MOVEs WS-MESSAGE to ERRMSGO, and
      *  issues EXEC CICS SEND MAP.  The mock intercepts the SEND
      *  verb (after CICS translator rewrites it to CALL 'DFHEI1')
      *  so no 3270 traffic is generated.
      *
      *  TC5 differs from TC3 in three meaningful ways:
      *    1. TC3 PERFORMs INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS DIRECTLY, isolating
      *       the leaf paragraph; TC5 PERFORMs the ORCHESTRATOR,
      *       proving the dispatch chain does not break.
      *    2. TC3 asserts VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES because the
      *       leaf paragraph contains no CICS verbs; TC5 asserts
      *       VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES because the
      *       orchestrator's second PERFORM reaches SEND-TRNVIEW-
      *       SCREEN's EXEC CICS SEND (count >= 1 on-platform).
      *    3. TC3 seeds 8 of the 14 input fields plus WS-MESSAGE;
      *       TC5 seeds a SMALLER subset (4 fields plus WS-MESSAGE)
      *       to focus the assertion on the orchestrator's
      *       end-to-end clear, not the leaf paragraph's exhaustive
      *       MOVE chain.  The smaller seed list also keeps the
      *       testcase below cobol-check's per-testcase line budget.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC5 prelude: seed TRNIDINI,
      *  CARDNUMI, TRNAMTI, MIDI, and WS-MESSAGE so the test proves
      *  that CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN's first PERFORM (INITIALIZE-ALL-
      *  FIELDS) reaches and executes its MOVE-TO-SPACES statements
      *  end-to-end.  Without these seeds the BEFORE-EACH initial
      *  state would already be SPACES and the test would not
      *  distinguish the orchestrator's effect from baseline.  The
      *  fields chosen represent each major category: a key field
      *  (TRNIDINI), a card-number key (CARDNUMI), a numeric-format
      *  field (TRNAMTI), a merchant id (MIDI), and the message
      *  slot (WS-MESSAGE).
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    SPACES - production literal MOVE'd by INITIALIZE-ALL-
      *             FIELDS lines 312-326; the test asserts the side
      *             effect (does NOT reimplement the MOVE)
      *    -1     - TRNIDINL flipped by production line 311, restoring
      *             the cursor-positioning default after the screen
      *             clear (a regression that drops line 311 from the
      *             production source would leave TRNIDINL at whatever
      *             value the prior SEND MAP set, breaking the BMS
      *             cursor positioning when the user re-enters the
      *             transaction id).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN01C CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN clears WS-MSG and map'
            MOVE 'OLDTXNID0000099 ' TO TRNIDINI OF COTRN1AI
            MOVE '5555555555554444' TO CARDNUMI OF COTRN1AI
            MOVE '+99999999.99' TO TRNAMTI OF COTRN1AI
            MOVE '999999999' TO MIDI OF COTRN1AI
            MOVE 'STALE MESSAGE FROM PRIOR FIXTURE' TO WS-MESSAGE
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN
            EXPECT TRNIDINI OF COTRN1AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT TRNIDINL OF COTRN1AI NOT = 0
            EXPECT CARDNUMI OF COTRN1AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT TRNAMTI OF COTRN1AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT MIDI OF COTRN1AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT WS-MESSAGE TO BE SPACES
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite COTRN01C TRANSACTION DETAIL VIEW
      ******************************************************************

